    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you on the integration part, but if you look at how these theories are actually applied, many argue that retributive-style punishment is just a way to preserve existing power hierarchies instead of actually fixing them. if the goal is \"progress,\" can we really call a system \"just\" if it still relies heavily on retributive principles, or is that just holding back the evolution you mentioned earlier?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
